  "slug": "crockpot-mississippi-cocktail-smokies-recipe-11902291",
  "name": "Crockpot Mississippi Cocktail Smokies",
  "recipe_type": "appetizer",
  "brief_description": "These Crockpot Mississippi cocktail smokies are rich and savory with a tangy, buttery sauce that clings to each bite. Ranch and au jus seasonings deepen umami and herbiness, while the pepperoncini add a bright, vinegary pop, and they are so easy to make.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Add sausages to a 4-quart slow cooker. Stir in Worcestershire sauce, 1/2 cup pepperoncini peppers, and pepperoncini liquid."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Evenly sprinkle au jus gravy mix, ranch seasoning, and garlic powder over sausages. Dot with butter, cover, and cook on Low until sausages are heated through and sauce is glossy, about 3 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Stir gently to evenly coat sausages. Stir in remaining 1/2 cup pepperoncini peppers. Serve warm."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 10,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 180,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 5,
